Drop the dynamic exception specification from the Config::parseStream
declaration. The .src.patch removes it from the definition in config.cpp, and
C++17 (gcc 14's default) rejects both the specification and a mismatch.
config.h is left out of cygport diff, hence the separate patch.

--- a/varconf/config.h
+++ b/varconf/config.h
@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ public:
 
   // Ensures specified filestream is properly formatted.
   // Why isn't this protected?
-  void parseStream(std::istream & in, Scope scope) throw (ParseError);
+  void parseStream(std::istream & in, Scope scope);
 
   // Wrapper for find(section)
   bool findSection(const std::string & section) const;
